# TreeSite Tile Rendering

- Keep standard sitemap nodes visually minimal: render a title and optional short description only.
- Do not add placeholder visuals, empty metadata areas, or dashboard-style card chrome to plain nodes.
- Rich tiles must opt in through explicit fields such as `template`, `image`, `links`, `url`, `embed`, `html`, or PDF document fields.
- PDF/document nodes should use `type: "pdf"` and `pdf: "/path/to/file.pdf"` or an imported asset URL.
- PDF tiles should render a visual first-page preview by default, use `previewImage` when provided, and fall back to a quiet PDF icon plus title if preview generation fails.
- Preserve the cinematic artifact style for document previews: edge-to-edge preview, soft rounded corners, subtle shadow, and title overlay gradient.
